    <briefdescription>
<para>Process-wide cache of the database schema used by the validators. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header declares the <ref refid="classDatabaseSchema" kindref="compound">DatabaseSchema</ref> class, which owns a single shared map describing every table and its columns. The map is filled once at server startup by asking <ref refid="classDatabaseController" kindref="compound">DatabaseController</ref> for the table list and each table&apos;s columns, and is read-only afterwards. It also defines SCHEMA_t, the convenient name for that map&apos;s type, used throughout the validator code.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: The validators need to know a table&apos;s columns and types to check client JSON, and querying the database on every request would be far too slow. This class provides that knowledge as a startup snapshot that <ref refid="classValidator" kindref="compound">Validator</ref> reads through getDatabaseSchema(). Without it, the validators would have no schema to compare against and would have to query the database on every create, update and read request.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Static data members / storage duration: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/storage_duration">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/storage_duration</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
